    "created_at": "2024-08-16T15:20:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-16T15:20:57Z",
    "body": "Performance will actually improve if an optional parameter is provided by parsers that would allow callers to request to fail early, so bogus URLs wouldn't have to be parsed fully because callers know that in their context tabs and newlines are not valid characters.\r\n\r\nThanks for your insights and guidance. It is much appreciated. Again, apologies for going down the rabbit hole with browsers.",
