    "updated_at": "2024-08-16T18:45:16Z",
    "body": "> I think it would also be unwise for Python to deviate from this as it would mean it ends up with different results from web browsers.\r\n\r\nNote that other software is _already_ more strict than web browsers, such as [curl](https://curl.se/) and [wget](https://www.gnu.org/software/wget/). And even browsers are not internally consistent, e.g. Firefox does not follow a [`Location: https://exa\tmple.com/` redirect](https://run.mocky.io/v3/abe4108f-192b-46a4-a6aa-7902802a7c1d) to https://example.com.",
